--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/7 + [class.base.init]/1: a mem-initializer-list pack
expansion `leaf<Ul, Tl>()...' over EMPTY packs Ul, Tl instantiates to no
mem-initializers at all.  libc++'s __tuple_impl constructor initializes
the elements given an argument with `__tuple_leaf<_Uf, _Tf>(std::forward<
_Up>(__u))...' and the rest with `__tuple_leaf<_Ul, _Tl>()...'; when every
element has an argument the second list is empty.  The front end still
instantiates one `leaf<?, int &&>()' default-constructing the reference
element ("reference 'this->value' expects one initializer"), drops the
leaf's default constructor, and symbolic execution then aborts with an
invariant violation ("symex_other.cpp: Unreachable").  In libc++ this is
tuple<int &&> from std::forward_as_tuple in map::operator[]
(`piecewise_construct, forward_as_tuple(key), tuple<>()'): __tuple_leaf
(tuple:320) is dropped in cpp11_libcxx20_map, cpp11_map_insert_libcxx and
cpp20_map_basic_libcxx (round-163 audit).  The empty-pack fix of round
163b covered braced lists and call arguments, not mem-initializers.
Header-free.  Pre-existing (round-162 snapshot bin51 fails the same way).
